# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for longcallD.
#
# klib's kt_for work stealing (src/kthread.c:29, steal_work) scans
# t->w[i].i without synchronisation to pick the worker with the least
# remaining work, then claims the item atomically with
# __sync_fetch_and_add and range-checks the result against t->n. A stale
# read can therefore only cause a suboptimal victim choice -- never an
# out-of-bounds index or a double-claimed item. This is upstream klib,
# byte-identical to the copy shipped in minimap2, and the racy read is
# deliberate. Suppressed rather than patched: editing vendored threading
# code to satisfy a sanitizer would be a worse trade than documenting it.
race:steal_work
